{"number": 16, "text": "                                                                                   Section A Letters and sounds\n\n\n         Exercises\n\n        First read this conversation to the end, and then write the letter or ‘p' in each gap.\n        Listen and check your answers.\n  All\n         Sip: Where  are the\n                 ears?!!! Did you  say .......ears?\n         Sip:              you  know,  fruit!\n        Jor:  Oh, I see, ......ears with a P! They’re in the ......ack.\n         Sip: What,  in the .......ack of the truck?\n        Jor:  No,  in the .......ack, you know, with a P!\n         Sip: Oh, I see, .......ack with a P! Would you like one?\n        Jor:  No,     have a  ......each, please.\n         Sip: A  beach?!!!\n\n          Follow up: Play the recording again, pausing it after each of lines.\n          You say Joe's lines before listening to him saying them.\n\n         The word ape  contains the two sounds /e1/ and /p/. If you reverse the sounds, you get the word\n         pay       Reverse the sounds in these words and  write the new word.\n         EXAMPLE    tops _\n\n         2                                                5 keeps\n\n\n         Listen. In one word in each group, the ‘b' or ‘p' is not pronounced. Circle the word.\n\n  Al2\n         EXAMPLE    double            Dublin\n                                                          5 recipe   repeat  receipt\n         1 lamb    label  lab\n                                                          6 possibly   psychology\n         2 crab   robbed    climb\n                                                          7 Cambridge     combine    combing\n         3 cup   cupboard     copy\n         4 photo    potato   paper\n\n         Listen and tick (W) the sentence you hear, A or B. If you find any of these difficult, go to\n         Section D4 Sound  pairs for further practice.\n  Al3\n\n                                                                  B\n   